{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_architecture_provenance_layer", "label": "ProvenanceLayer Type", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "5.2 Provenance model", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Four layers (scientific-data, rendered-visualization, derived, synthetic) are never merged, so derived data cannot silently become 'raw'."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_data_status", "label": "DataStatus Type", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "5.2 Provenance model", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Availability is independent of provenance: a dataset can be scientifically real and still be not-connected, which is exactly the ECCO2 state."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_scientific_variable", "label": "ScientificVariable Contract", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "5.3 Scientific contracts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Units are explicit with `unknown` rather than guessing, and validRange must name its source."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_scientific_dataset", "label": "ScientificDataset Contract", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "5.3 Scientific contracts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_normalized_sample", "label": "NormalizedSample Contract", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "5.3 Scientific contracts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A normalized sample retains the original sourceValue so the audio value can always be traced back to the data value."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_scientific_frame", "label": "ScientificFrame Contract", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "5.3 Scientific contracts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_normalization", "label": "Normalization Functions (normalizeLinear / normalizeLog)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "5.4 Normalization", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Returns null for non-finite input, zero-width ranges, non-positive log values, and invalid ranges; null means 'no audio value' and must not be replaced with zero because zero is a real data value. Deliberately free of dataset-specific constants."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_nasa_svs_client", "label": "NASA SVS API Client (server-only, unused)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "5.5 NASA API client", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Exists so a future acquisition job has one controlled entry point instead of ad-hoc fetches in components; `import \"server-only\"` prevents client bundling, and it is not called in Stage 1 so the demo does not depend on a government server at runtime."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_audio_boundary", "label": "Audio Boundary (SonificationEngine interfaces)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "6 Audio boundary", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A mapping is an inspectable scientific claim; physical ranges live on the scientific variable rather than the audio mapping; the scene owns time, not the UI; AudioContext is created only after a user gesture, and AUDIO_STATUS encodes the honest current state."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_route_explore", "label": "Explore Route (/)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "4 Route composition", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Renders title block, plate, disabled transport, then rail so evidence is read after the image but before any control; VisualizationPlate is the only client component because it tracks image load state."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_accessibility", "label": "Accessibility Implementation", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "8 Accessibility", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stage 1 must already be keyboard-operable, screen-reader legible, reduced-motion aware, and free of color-only status; disabled controls expose their reason through visible text and aria-describedby. No formal WCAG audit is claimed."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_stage_2_extension_points", "label": "Stage 2 Extension Points (5 steps)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "11 Stage 2 extension points", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ordered path: acquire a defensible subset, convert to a browser contract, normalize and map, implement the Web Audio engine, then add equivalent non-audio state. validRange must come from dataset metadata, never from a rendered image."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_design_tokens", "label": "CSS Design Tokens (globals.css)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "7 Design system", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All visual decisions live as CSS custom properties plus component classes; Tailwind is present but utility classes are avoided for the core instrument layout because the brief required a precise, non-generic composition."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_architecture_provenance_layer", "target": "docs_architecture_data_status", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED"